<title>USA: Detroit Edison says Fermi nuke at 18 pct.</title>
<headline>Detroit Edison says Fermi nuke at 18 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Detroit Edison's 1,116 megawatt Fermi 2 nuclear unit is operating at about 18 percent power is expected to return to the electricity grid &quot;in the next couple of days,&quot; a company spokesman said Friday.</p>
<p>The unit, in Newport, Mich., automatically shut down Saturday due to problems with instrumentation on the plant's backfill system.</p>
<p>Detroit Edison, which owns and operates Fermi 2, is a subsidiary of DTE Energy Corp.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
